a venereum among men who have sex with men&#x02014;the Netherlands; 2003&#x02013;2004.</article-title><source>MMWR Morb Mortal Wkly Rep</source> <year>2004</year>;<volume>53</volume>:<fpage>985</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>8</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15514580</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="R12"><label>12. </label><citation citation-type="journal"><string-name><surname>G&#x000f6;tz</surname> <given-names>HM</given-names></string-name> <article-title>van Doornum, Niesters HG, den Hollander JG, Thio HB, de Zwart O. A cluster of acute hepatitis C virus infection among men who have sex with men&#x02013;results from contact tracing and public health implications.</article-title><source>AIDS</source> <year>2005</year>;<volume>19</volume>:<fpage>969</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>74</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15905679</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="R13"><label>13. </label><citation citation-type="web"><string-name><surname>Vall Mayans</surname> <given-names>M</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>Sanz Colomo</surname> <given-names>B</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>Ossewaarde</surname> <given-names>J</given-names></string-name> First case of LGV confirmed in Barcelona. Euro Surveill. <year>2005</year>;10:E050203.2 [cited 2006 Oct 19]. Available from <ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://www.eurosurveillance.org/ew/2005/050203.asp#2">http://www.eurosurveillance.org/ew/2005/050203.asp#2</ext-link></citation></ref><ref id="R14"><label>14. </label><citation citation-type="web"><string-name><surname>van de Laar</surname> <given-names>M</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>Fenton</surname> <given-names>K</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>Ison</surname> <given-names>C</given-names></string-name> European Surveillance of Sexually Transmitted Infections (ESSTI). Update on the European lymphogranuloma venereum epidemic among men who have sex with men. Euro Surveill. <year>2005</year>;10(6):E050602.1 [cite